---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & Sources"
  description="About the Rural HF Pocket Guide, author, sources, and how to cite."
  pageId="about"
>
  <header class="mb-6">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[color:var(--color-alert-deep)]">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">About this guide</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="prose max-w-none space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
    <p>
      The <strong>Rural HF Pocket Guide</strong> is a free, zero-login clinical reference for
      primary care clinicians managing heart failure in rural and resource-limited US settings.
      All content mirrors the <strong>HEARTLAND Implementation Toolkit V3.3</strong> (Heart failure
      Evidence-based Access in Rural Treatment, Linking Advanced Network Delivery), deposited on
      Zenodo in 2026 and described in a separate peer-reviewed technical report in
      <em>Cureus</em> (2026).
    </p>
    <p>
      This guide is a <em>reference-only</em> PWA. It does not accept patient input, track
      identifiable data, or replace the interactive <a href="https://heartlandprotocol.org">HEARTLAND app</a>
      (which offers risk-score calculation, titration workflows, and reporting for registered
      clinicians).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8">
    <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Sources &amp; DOIs</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
      <li class="rounded border border-[color:var(--color-grid)] bg-white p-3">
        <strong>This guide (Zenodo)</strong> — Rural HF Pocket Guide, v0.1.0 (software), 2026.
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19634993" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19634993
        </a>
        (all versions: 10.5281/zenodo.19634992)
      </li>
      <li class="rounded border border-[color:var(--color-grid)] bg-white p-3">
        <strong>Implementation toolkit (Zenodo)</strong> — Muller Ferreira V. HEARTLAND
        Implementation Toolkit V3.3, 2026.
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19101219" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19101219
        </a>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded border border-[color:var(--color-grid)] bg-white p-3">
        <strong>Peer-reviewed article</strong> — Muller Ferreira V. <em>Cureus</em>, 2026.
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.7759/cureus.104817" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          doi.org/10.7759/cureus.104817
        </a>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded border border-[color:var(--color-grid)] bg-white p-3">
        <strong>OSF deposit</strong> —
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.17605/OSF.IO/YUSGH" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          doi.org/10.17605/OSF.IO/YUSGH
        </a>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded border border-[color:var(--color-grid)] bg-white p-3">
        <strong>HEARTLAND app (interactive)</strong> —
        <a href="https://heartlandprotocol.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">heartlandprotocol.org</a>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded border border-[color:var(--color-grid)] bg-white p-3">
        <strong>Source repository</strong> —
        <a href="https://github.com/vickymuller-md/heartland-pocket-guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          github.com/vickymuller-md/heartland-pocket-guide
        </a>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded border border-[color:var(--color-grid)] bg-white p-3">
        <strong>Software Heritage snapshot</strong> —
        <a href="https://archive.softwareheritage.org/swh:1:snp:6f3d4e96dcde1ebeffa2b7e05865facf6c87a6e5/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          swh:1:snp:6f3d4e96dcde1ebeffa2b7e05865facf6c87a6e5
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8">
    <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Author</h2>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <strong>Vicky Muller Ferreira, MD</strong> — ORCID
      <a href="https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1099-5690" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        0009-0009-1099-5690
